WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:04.178 --> 00:00:07.442
And this is where the
magic really happens.

2
00:00:07.572 --> 00:00:09.532
If you look to your right.
you will see the office

3
00:00:09.661 --> 00:00:11.533
of the man himself.

4
00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:14.579
our host. Scotty Bristol.

5
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.930
He's probably in there right
now. going over material.

6
00:00:18.061 --> 00:00:21.499
preparing for tonight's show.
which tapes in a few hours.

7
00:00:21.586 --> 00:00:23.501
What do you say we
say a quick hello?

8
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.940
Actually. I-I think I'll
keep my job instead.

9
00:00:29.464 --> 00:00:32.162
A-And right next door
is the writers room.

10
00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:34.730
where. uh. Scotty's
hilarious monologues

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.472
and comedy bits are born.

12
00:00:37.602 --> 00:00:39.082
The writers are waiting to hear

13
00:00:39.213 --> 00:00:41.389
if their material
made the final cut.

14
00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.870
He hated it.

15
00:00:45.001 --> 00:00:46.698
Monologue or the mayor bit?

16
00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:48.309
All of it. Every line.

17
00:00:48.396 --> 00:00:50.396
But we stayed late last
night. That was good stuff.

18
00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:52.748
Are you sure you
pitched it right?

19
00:00:52.922 --> 00:00:54.793
Yes. Ronan. I know how to pitch.

20
00:00:54.924 --> 00:00:56.621
I come from a comedy background.

21
00:00:56.708 --> 00:00:58.145
-Improv.
-Improv.

22
00:00:58.275 --> 00:00:59.759
Look. he just didn't
like it. It happens.

23
00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:01.583
Okay. but what kind
of mood was he in?

24
00:01:01.713 --> 00:01:03.502
Because you also have to
pick the right moment.

25
00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:05.413
Because it's our job
as women to always

26
00:01:05.543 --> 00:01:08.372
ascertain a man's emotional
state before speaking.

27
00:01:08.503 --> 00:01:10.074
Look. go ahead and blame
me. I'm used to it.

28
00:01:10.157 --> 00:01:11.767
But the material isn't
going in the show.

29
00:01:11.897 --> 00:01:13.769
And we know where it is going.

30
00:01:16.424 --> 00:01:20.254
Ugh. yes. the dulcet
tones of Mickey Two.

31
00:01:20.384 --> 00:01:22.952
Okay. so. our stuff
went in the shredder.

32
00:01:23.126 --> 00:01:24.606
What'll he use instead?

33
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.303
He's going to the packets.

34
00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.871
--For the love of comedy!
-Oh. no!

35
00:01:29.001 --> 00:01:31.352
-This is your fault.
-Oh. no. come on!

36
00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:33.745
Whose side are you on?

37
00:01:35.878 --> 00:01:37.532
Hi. Sheryl.

38
00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:40.883
I'm Laurel. head writer.
executive producer of Way Late.

39
00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.667
-Are you nervous?
-Oh. God.

40
00:01:42.841 --> 00:01:44.321
is it that obvious?

41
00:01:44.452 --> 00:01:47.542
It's just... network
television.

42
00:01:47.628 --> 00:01:49.892
I'm old enough that
still means something.

43
00:01:50.021 --> 00:01:51.781
Well. our
audience feels the same.

44
00:01:51.894 --> 00:01:53.420
-Oh. Okay.
-So. here are some questions

45
00:01:53.503 --> 00:01:55.419
that Scotty may or may not ask.

46
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.639
Do you think that
he'll be nice to me?

47
00:01:57.769 --> 00:02:00.772
I mean. I know sometimes he
can be a little bit acerbic...

48
00:02:00.903 --> 00:02:03.384
That's a lie! I'm always nice.

49
00:02:03.514 --> 00:02:05.734
Oh. my God! You're... so
much taller in person.

50
00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:08.039
Well. that depends on
the size of your screen.

51
00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.259
-Hi. Sheryl. Nice to meet you.
-Hi.

52
00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.305
Hey. listen. it's
gonna be a lot of fun.

53
00:02:11.435 --> 00:02:12.828
Just relax and be yourself.

54
00:02:12.915 --> 00:02:14.917
I actually brought a
friend for support.

55
00:02:15.047 --> 00:02:17.572
Elsbeth? Elsbeth!

56
00:02:17.702 --> 00:02:19.965
What?! Oh. Hi! Yes. I'm here.

57
00:02:20.096 --> 00:02:22.490
Uh. Elsbeth
was my journey partner

58
00:02:22.664 --> 00:02:24.013
at one of the wellness centers

59
00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:25.323
-I wrote about.
-Hi. Elsbeth.

60
00:02:25.406 --> 00:02:26.668
I hope I'm saying that right.

61
00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:27.847
'cause I won't be
saying it again.

62
00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.932
Oh. my gosh. it's you.

63
00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:31.151
I can't believe it.

64
00:02:31.238 --> 00:02:32.456
Oh. I am such a fan.

65
00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.110
You're so tall.

66
00:02:34.284 --> 00:02:36.073
Yeah. we established that
while you were unconscious.

67
00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.418
Yeah... Oh. right.

68
00:02:37.548 --> 00:02:38.941
Sorry. Um...

69
00:02:39.071 --> 00:02:40.381
I came straight here
from the airport.

70
00:02:40.464 --> 00:02:42.379
I was in Scotland
visiting Angus.

71
00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:43.859
Uh. my boyfriend.

72
00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.166
Uh. actually... I am not sure

73
00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.343
I should call him
that. but. um. anyway.

74
00:02:49.473 --> 00:02:52.737
I am jet-lagged. which is
why I seem a little loopy.

75
00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:54.348
although some people think...

76
00:02:54.478 --> 00:02:56.263
I always
seem a little loopy.

77
00:02:56.393 --> 00:02:58.221
You know what's fascinating
about that story?

78
00:02:58.308 --> 00:02:59.701
I didn't ask.

79
00:02:59.831 --> 00:03:02.051
-See you out there.
-Okay.

80
00:03:04.836 --> 00:03:06.664
Uh. okay. Okay.

81
00:03:06.751 --> 00:03:08.710
-Oh...
-You got this.

82
00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.842
-Is there coffee?
-Yeah.

83
00:03:11.016 --> 00:03:13.193
Get her a decaf!

84
00:03:16.152 --> 00:03:18.850
Hey. everybody. Welcome
back to Way Late.

85
00:03:18.937 --> 00:03:20.504
We are talking to Sheryl Jacobs.

86
00:03:20.678 --> 00:03:23.855
the author of Unwell on My Way.

87
00:03:23.942 --> 00:03:25.857
So. Sheryl. it says in here that

88
00:03:25.988 --> 00:03:28.120
you went from wellness
center to wellness center

89
00:03:28.295 --> 00:03:29.644
for four full years.

90
00:03:29.731 --> 00:03:31.950
Four years and three months.

91
00:03:32.081 --> 00:03:34.281
You must have had a lot of
junk mail when you came home.

92
00:03:34.649 --> 00:03:36.999
Oh.
Yeah. I...

93
00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:38.783
I mentioned that in the book.

94
00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.437
Didn't you read it?

95
00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:42.744
Well. I have to read a
lot for this job. Sheryl.

96
00:03:42.874 --> 00:03:45.703
Oh. right. Is that hard for you?

97
00:03:46.748 --> 00:03:48.793
Mickey. Sheryl's
being mean to me.

98
00:03:48.966 --> 00:03:50.230
Hey. did you meet Mickey Muntz?

99
00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.189
Oh. no. but I-I know
him from the show.

100
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.452
Good to meet you.
Sheryl. I loved your book

101
00:03:55.539 --> 00:03:58.368
-and I read every word of it.
-Oh...

102
00:03:58.499 --> 00:04:00.179
Hey. uh. listen. let
me ask you something.

103
00:04:00.631 --> 00:04:02.115
Uh. what wellness
treatment do you think

104
00:04:02.198 --> 00:04:03.464
would be good for
Mickey over there?

105
00:04:03.547 --> 00:04:05.201
I mean. obviously.
he needs all of 'em.

106
00:04:05.332 --> 00:04:06.685
but what would you
start with first...

107
00:04:06.768 --> 00:04:08.422
the weight or the
air of desperation?

108
00:04:08.552 --> 00:04:10.075
Well. um.

109
00:04:10.206 --> 00:04:11.251
I think focusing

110
00:04:11.381 --> 00:04:13.122
on the. um. spiritual.

111
00:04:13.296 --> 00:04:15.298
uh. being is always first.

112
00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:17.039
and then the physical.

113
00:04:17.213 --> 00:04:18.262
Well. that's good to know.
'cause we don't want to focus

114
00:04:18.345 --> 00:04:20.172
on Mickey's physical being.

115
00:04:20.303 --> 00:04:23.350
Yes. and my spirit
is definitely broken.

116
00:04:25.047 --> 00:04:26.661
Anyway. this has
been. uh. great. Sheryl.

117
00:04:26.744 --> 00:04:27.793
Would you please come back?

118
00:04:27.876 --> 00:04:29.094
Is that it?

119
00:04:29.225 --> 00:04:29.921
-That's it.
-Um. sure...

120
00:04:30.095 --> 00:04:31.749
It is way late.-♪

121
00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:33.142
Go to sleep. everybody.

122
00:04:33.316 --> 00:04:35.623
Bye-bye.

123
00:04:43.413 --> 00:04:44.413
Well?

124
00:04:44.545 --> 00:04:46.677
-He said no.
-Are you kidding me?

125
00:04:46.808 --> 00:04:48.418
Sweetheart.

126
00:04:48.549 --> 00:04:50.115
Did you tell him
what the doctor said?

127
00:04:50.246 --> 00:04:52.074
-I did.
-Word for word?

128
00:04:52.204 --> 00:04:53.728
-Honey.
-Mickey. your heart

129
00:04:53.815 --> 00:04:55.599
is in bad shape. If
you don't get a break

130
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.690
from the stress... taking
his abuse every night...

131
00:04:57.819 --> 00:04:59.734
who knows what could happen?

132
00:04:59.864 --> 00:05:02.650
Look. you push me to get a
mammogram once a year. and I do.

133
00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.652
and I love you for
taking care of me.

134
00:05:04.782 --> 00:05:07.045
Now. I'm asking you to
take care of yourself.

135
00:05:07.176 --> 00:05:08.438
He said it was impossible.

136
00:05:08.569 --> 00:05:10.353
The ratings are down
and he's got Ronan

137
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.964
waiting in the wings
to take his place.

138
00:05:13.051 --> 00:05:14.966
This is the job I signed up for.

139
00:05:15.097 --> 00:05:16.838
God. he's killing you.

140
00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:17.926
How dare he?

141
00:05:18.013 --> 00:05:20.276
I'll be fine.

142
00:05:20.407 --> 00:05:22.757
Look. we owe Scotty so much.

143
00:05:22.844 --> 00:05:23.964
We'd be nothing without him.

144
00:05:24.062 --> 00:05:25.629
Oh. I don't believe that.

145
00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.935
No. you're right.

146
00:05:27.065 --> 00:05:28.371
I'd be nothing without him.

147
00:05:28.502 --> 00:05:30.025
I mean. you could be anything.

148
00:05:30.112 --> 00:05:32.636
Oh. Mickey. You're
such a good person.

149
00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.770
Yeah. but I wanted to
be in show business.

150
00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.425
Get changed and go home.

151
00:05:38.599 --> 00:05:40.165
I'm gonna watch the edit.

152
00:05:40.296 --> 00:05:41.689
Not that they know I'm there.

153
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:49.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

154
00:05:51.394 --> 00:05:52.704
What would you
start with first...

155
00:05:52.787 --> 00:05:54.397
the weight or the
air of desperation?

156
00:05:54.484 --> 00:05:57.487
-Bump me that close-up.
-Yep.

157
00:06:14.461 --> 00:06:16.158
I figured he would send you.

158
00:06:16.288 --> 00:06:18.073
He told you what
the doctors said?

159
00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.249
Doctors?
Are we still doing doctors?

160
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.687
Scotty. this show is
literally killing him.

161
00:06:23.818 --> 00:06:26.429
But we'll miss it
when it's gone.

162
00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.779
Yeah. yeah. I know.

163
00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.391
This show is what the
three of us dreamed about.

164
00:06:31.521 --> 00:06:33.745
-and we have to live with the choices that we made...
-Right.

165
00:06:33.828 --> 00:06:35.743
-and you chose Mickey.
-I did.

166
00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:36.700
Any regrets?

167
00:06:36.874 --> 00:06:38.702
Only when I watch the show.

168
00:06:38.832 --> 00:06:41.096
Cute. What about kids?

169
00:06:41.226 --> 00:06:43.272
No. no. no. you were
right about that.

170
00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:44.799
You know. we would have
never have gotten this far

171
00:06:44.882 --> 00:06:46.493
if we had to split our focus.

172
00:06:47.972 --> 00:06:49.278
Drink?

173
00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.759
Uh... yeah.

174
00:06:54.544 --> 00:06:56.333
I was thinking about
that night the scout came

175
00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:58.853
from the network to see
our show for the first time

176
00:06:58.983 --> 00:07:01.163
and someone from the audience
called out "Renaissance fair"

177
00:07:01.246 --> 00:07:02.552
as a suggestion.

178
00:07:02.683 --> 00:07:04.293
So we're walking
down memory lane now.

179
00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:06.426
And you had that
Renaissance fair bit

180
00:07:06.513 --> 00:07:08.428
from the week
before that killed.

181
00:07:08.602 --> 00:07:10.691
It was ready to go. making
you look like a star.

182
00:07:12.693 --> 00:07:15.739
Now. the guy who called
it out was a plant. right?

183
00:07:15.913 --> 00:07:18.960
Laurel. good luck
comes from preparation.

184
00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.179
Yeah. You know. it's funny...

185
00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.879
I think I chose Mickey
over you that night.

186
00:07:25.009 --> 00:07:28.535
Your ambition scared
the hell out of me.

187
00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.713
Gosh. what was I so afraid of?

188
00:07:49.773 --> 00:07:51.819
-Laurel.
-Mm-hmm?

189
00:07:51.949 --> 00:07:53.255
-What are you doing?
-Just

190
00:07:53.429 --> 00:07:55.387
making it look better.
you know? Sexier.

191
00:07:55.518 --> 00:07:57.085
Are we...

192
00:07:58.216 --> 00:07:59.609
Are we really gonna do this?

193
00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.393
Doing what? I'm
just having a drink

194
00:08:01.568 --> 00:08:03.352
with an old friend.

195
00:08:03.439 --> 00:08:07.008
Don't you miss the way
it felt. before all this?

196
00:08:08.052 --> 00:08:10.141
-Well. of course.
-Mm.

197
00:08:10.272 --> 00:08:12.187
I mean. some nights. I...

198
00:08:12.274 --> 00:08:14.276
look over at you and...

199
00:08:14.406 --> 00:08:16.670
and I'm right back there.

200
00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.715
the three of us on
stage. making it up

201
00:08:18.802 --> 00:08:20.587
-as we go along. you know?
-Yeah.

202
00:08:20.717 --> 00:08:23.241
So in tune with each other.

203
00:08:24.286 --> 00:08:25.548
So young.

204
00:08:26.549 --> 00:08:29.465
You haven't changed.
Come with me.

205
00:08:30.248 --> 00:08:31.554
What-What's... Okay.

206
00:08:31.685 --> 00:08:33.207
Yeah. all right.
No. I'm into it.

207
00:08:33.381 --> 00:08:36.167
-Um... all right. yeah.
-Mm.

208
00:08:36.298 --> 00:08:37.956
I've
been nothing but loyal to you.

209
00:08:38.039 --> 00:08:39.126
and Laurel has. too.

210
00:08:39.256 --> 00:08:41.607
Uh. and-and I deserve this.

211
00:08:41.738 --> 00:08:44.654
My health is more
important than some show.

212
00:08:44.741 --> 00:08:46.874
Look. Laurel. I just
want you to know

213
00:08:47.004 --> 00:08:48.440
I've always
respected and admired

214
00:08:48.615 --> 00:08:51.182
-how loyal you are to Mickey.
-I know.

215
00:08:51.269 --> 00:08:53.402
But I guess. um...

216
00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:54.795
even you have your limits.

217
00:08:54.969 --> 00:08:56.927
Guess I do.

218
00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:58.712
Aah!

219
00:09:25.652 --> 00:09:28.655
Scotty. I can't do this anymore.

220
00:09:28.785 --> 00:09:30.439
Scotty?

221
00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.093
Scotty!

222
00:09:34.617 --> 00:09:36.227
Was that a scream?

223
00:09:41.842 --> 00:09:43.325
Mom. I thought you weren't
supposed to be home

224
00:09:43.408 --> 00:09:44.714
for another few days.

225
00:09:44.801 --> 00:09:46.198
Did things with
Angus not go so well?

226
00:09:46.281 --> 00:09:48.762
No. Sheryl asked me to
go to the show with her

227
00:09:48.892 --> 00:09:51.503
and then to dinner. and I want
to be supportive of my friends.

228
00:09:51.678 --> 00:09:53.593
especially now that Kaya's off

229
00:09:53.723 --> 00:09:56.247
-working undercover.
-Are we sure that's the reason?

230
00:09:56.378 --> 00:09:58.293
There she is!

231
00:09:58.423 --> 00:10:00.164
Oh. my Gonzo!

232
00:10:00.295 --> 00:10:02.340
I missed you so much.

233
00:10:02.514 --> 00:10:03.994
-Were you a good girl?
-Easy peasy.

234
00:10:04.125 --> 00:10:05.434
-Oh. Teddy. Teddy. I have gifts.
-Okay. Mom.

235
00:10:05.517 --> 00:10:06.910
-let me. You're exhausted.
-Okay.

236
00:10:07.041 --> 00:10:09.130
Thank you. sweetheart. Yeah.
the-the one on the top.

237
00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.435
Yeah. that's for Gonzo.

238
00:10:10.566 --> 00:10:11.436
-Yeah. There you go!
-Oh!

239
00:10:11.523 --> 00:10:12.742
Go get it. girl!

240
00:10:12.873 --> 00:10:14.309
And that's for you and Roy.

241
00:10:14.439 --> 00:10:16.311
You got us tartan kilts.

242
00:10:16.441 --> 00:10:18.748
Yeah. you both have
such nice calves.

243
00:10:18.879 --> 00:10:21.185
Oh. thanks. That's fun.

244
00:10:21.316 --> 00:10:22.796
Although...

245
00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:24.624
I think it's probably
a little too soon

246
00:10:24.754 --> 00:10:26.626
for me to wear
these at my new job.

247
00:10:26.756 --> 00:10:29.324
Yeah. probably. Wait. what?

248
00:10:29.411 --> 00:10:31.369
Teddy! You got a job?

249
00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.067
-Shocking. I know.
-Oh!

250
00:10:33.154 --> 00:10:36.113
Well. Roy and I were at this
bar and we met this reporter.

251
00:10:36.244 --> 00:10:38.768
and I started going on about
how the truth has been devalued

252
00:10:38.855 --> 00:10:40.078
and the world needs
more fact-checkers.

253
00:10:40.161 --> 00:10:41.858
-Oh. that's so true.
-And before I knew it.

254
00:10:41.989 --> 00:10:43.255
you know. I was hired
at The New York View.

255
00:10:43.338 --> 00:10:44.430
Did you know one of
their journalists

256
00:10:44.513 --> 00:10:45.605
got murdered with a cattle prod?

257
00:10:45.688 --> 00:10:46.515
Mm-hmm. That's how we got Gonzo.

258
00:10:46.689 --> 00:10:48.299
-What?
-Uh. long story.

259
00:10:48.386 --> 00:10:50.088
Anyway. I really do think
that investigative journalism

260
00:10:50.171 --> 00:10:52.347
could be the path for me.
Did you know that Chris Hayes

261
00:10:52.477 --> 00:10:54.044
was a philosophy
major just like I was?

262
00:10:54.218 --> 00:10:55.876
-I think I did know that.
-And the best part is that

263
00:10:55.959 --> 00:10:57.308
print media is a dying business.

264
00:10:57.439 --> 00:10:59.659
and so the bar to
entry is really low.

265
00:10:59.833 --> 00:11:02.966
Mm. that's wonderful.
honey. I'm so...

266
00:11:03.053 --> 00:11:05.577
-Okay. Mom. you need to sleep.
-Oh... Oh. gosh.

267
00:11:05.752 --> 00:11:07.318
No! I want to stay up.

268
00:11:07.449 --> 00:11:08.580
I have to watch Way Late.

269
00:11:08.755 --> 00:11:10.017
I have to see if I see myself

270
00:11:10.191 --> 00:11:11.148
in the audience.

271
00:11:11.235 --> 00:11:13.063
Um. Mom. I think the show

272
00:11:13.194 --> 00:11:14.369
may be preempted.

273
00:11:14.499 --> 00:11:16.110
Oh. no. What happened?
Is it Greenland?

274
00:11:20.854 --> 00:11:22.594
Oh. Hello?

275
00:11:22.725 --> 00:11:26.207
Elsbeth. Oh. good.
you made it home.

276
00:11:26.337 --> 00:11:27.774
And you're still awake.

277
00:11:42.876 --> 00:11:44.529
Oh. Captain Wagner.

278
00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:46.575
Here I am. across
several time zones.

279
00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:48.055
reporting for duty.

280
00:11:48.185 --> 00:11:50.057
I'm glad you came back
early. I need you here.

281
00:11:50.231 --> 00:11:52.624
Talk about a high-profile case.

282
00:11:52.755 --> 00:11:55.192
Yeah. I see Detective Smullen.

283
00:11:55.279 --> 00:11:58.456
Is there an officer assigned
to "keep me in line"?

284
00:11:58.587 --> 00:12:01.198
Yes. you'll be working
with Officer Grace Hackett.

285
00:12:01.285 --> 00:12:02.852
who's particularly
well-suited for this.

286
00:12:03.026 --> 00:12:04.245
Oh. Why is that?

287
00:12:04.375 --> 00:12:05.812
Well. I happen to
know she's a. uh.

288
00:12:05.899 --> 00:12:07.596
stand-up comic in
her spare time.

289
00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:10.642
Ooh. that ought to be
helpful. And good for laughs.

290
00:12:10.773 --> 00:12:13.558
Where is she? Oh. I see. Um...

291
00:12:13.645 --> 00:12:16.039
Hi. Officer Hackett? Hi.

292
00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.302
Oh. gosh.

293
00:12:18.433 --> 00:12:20.526
I'm sorry. I didn't realize
you were having a moment there.

294
00:12:20.609 --> 00:12:21.871
No.

295
00:12:22.002 --> 00:12:23.094
-I'm...
-Yeah. I-I know who you are.

296
00:12:23.177 --> 00:12:24.439
I'm sorry.

297
00:12:24.569 --> 00:12:26.049
I always dreamed of being here.

298
00:12:26.223 --> 00:12:28.008
in this office. and. um...

299
00:12:28.138 --> 00:12:31.098
this is just not the way
I wanted to get here.

300
00:12:31.272 --> 00:12:32.752
-you know?
-Y-Yeah.

301
00:12:34.057 --> 00:12:35.755
Oh. I'm sorry. I'm an empath.

302
00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:38.235
That's okay.

303
00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:40.281
It's nice.

304
00:12:40.455 --> 00:12:42.457
According to Mickey Muntz.

305
00:12:42.631 --> 00:12:44.111
our sidekick who found the body.

306
00:12:44.285 --> 00:12:46.156
Scotty Bristol was
famous for feeding

307
00:12:46.287 --> 00:12:47.679
material that he didn't like

308
00:12:47.854 --> 00:12:50.073
into this industrial
monster over here

309
00:12:50.247 --> 00:12:51.640
just to. uh. piss
off the writers.

310
00:12:51.814 --> 00:12:53.555
-God. this business.
-Yeah.

311
00:12:53.729 --> 00:12:56.036
We're bagging what's in
the bin for evidence.

312
00:12:56.165 --> 00:12:58.081
but it's looking like
a pretty unfortunate

313
00:12:58.212 --> 00:13:00.823
necktie shredding accident.

314
00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.304
Were these his earbuds?

315
00:13:03.434 --> 00:13:04.566
So we assume.

316
00:13:04.696 --> 00:13:06.263
Do we know what he
was listening to?

317
00:13:07.308 --> 00:13:10.877
Merrily We Roll Along.
original cast recording.

318
00:13:11.051 --> 00:13:13.053
Your
guess is as good as mine.

319
00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.316
Oh. I think my guess
is probably better.

320
00:13:15.446 --> 00:13:17.709
Sondheim's score
is a masterpiece.

321
00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.929
And the story is told backwards.

322
00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:22.149
which always made
perfect sense to me.

323
00:13:22.279 --> 00:13:23.106
Yeah. me too.

324
00:13:23.237 --> 00:13:25.021
So...

325
00:13:25.152 --> 00:13:28.198
he was strangled by his...

326
00:13:28.285 --> 00:13:30.157
tie?

327
00:13:30.287 --> 00:13:32.899
Mm. so that means his
back was to the shredder.

328
00:13:33.029 --> 00:13:34.552
Why would that be?

329
00:13:34.683 --> 00:13:36.293
Maybe he turned to get away.

330
00:13:36.424 --> 00:13:37.468
Uh. well...

331
00:13:37.599 --> 00:13:39.906
Mm.

332
00:13:40.036 --> 00:13:43.039
But his tie would have
had to be on tight.

333
00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.215
otherwise he'd be able
to pull it off in time.

334
00:13:45.346 --> 00:13:48.131
But Scotty always
loosened his tie

335
00:13:48.262 --> 00:13:49.654
at the end of every show.

336
00:13:49.785 --> 00:13:51.700
"It's
way late. Go to sleep."

337
00:13:51.787 --> 00:13:53.702
Yeah. that was a signature move.

338
00:13:53.789 --> 00:13:55.589
Are there any prints?

339
00:13:56.313 --> 00:13:58.272
Uh. none that we found so far.

340
00:13:58.359 --> 00:14:00.143
Hmm. Ooh!

341
00:14:00.274 --> 00:14:02.319
There's a "jam override" button.

342
00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.105
That means the shredder
shuts off when it gets jammed

343
00:14:05.235 --> 00:14:07.411
with too much paper or...

344
00:14:07.585 --> 00:14:09.631
the body of a talk show
host.

345
00:14:09.761 --> 00:14:11.589
So. that means somebody

346
00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:13.678
had to push that button

347
00:14:13.765 --> 00:14:15.942
to keep it going. And. look...

348
00:14:16.072 --> 00:14:17.508
there's a "reverse" button.

349
00:14:17.639 --> 00:14:18.988
So...

350
00:14:20.381 --> 00:14:21.948
...why didn't Scotty
just push that?

351
00:14:23.079 --> 00:14:24.211
Reverse button?

352
00:14:24.341 --> 00:14:26.169
Scotty never changed his mind.

353
00:14:26.343 --> 00:14:27.518
Laurel. right?

354
00:14:27.649 --> 00:14:28.911
We met in the green room.

355
00:14:28.998 --> 00:14:30.221
I was here with
my friend Sheryl.

356
00:14:30.304 --> 00:14:32.610
Oh. Jet lag.

357
00:14:32.784 --> 00:14:34.134
Still got it.

358
00:14:34.221 --> 00:14:36.353
Well. I'd really like to
take my husband home now.

359
00:14:36.484 --> 00:14:37.789
He has a heart condition.

360
00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:39.790
-Let's go.
-Oh. Of course. Uh. just...

361
00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:41.881
Can I just ask on question?
Do you have any idea

362
00:14:42.055 --> 00:14:44.448
what Scotty might
have been shredding?

363
00:14:44.622 --> 00:14:46.668
Some material he
didn't like. probably?

364
00:14:46.798 --> 00:14:48.365
-Let's go.
-Huh. That's...

365
00:14:48.539 --> 00:14:50.150
odd.

366
00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.152
Because Mickey said that Scotty

367
00:14:52.239 --> 00:14:53.839
used the shredder to
torture the writers.

368
00:14:53.936 --> 00:14:55.677
but the writers were
gone for the day.

369
00:14:55.807 --> 00:14:58.680
weren't they? So the...

370
00:14:58.854 --> 00:15:00.900
...would be lost on them.

371
00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:03.206
I-I guess we'll never
know what he was thinking.

372
00:15:03.337 --> 00:15:04.294
He was here alone.

373
00:15:04.381 --> 00:15:05.817
Or maybe not.

374
00:15:07.123 --> 00:15:08.385
'Cause Scotty...

375
00:15:08.516 --> 00:15:09.996
took out his earbuds.

376
00:15:10.126 --> 00:15:11.867
but he didn't put
them back in the case.

377
00:15:11.998 --> 00:15:14.739
as if he was expecting to
put them back in his ear

378
00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:18.004
after some brief
interruption. like to. um...

379
00:15:18.134 --> 00:15:19.179
talk to someone.

380
00:15:19.309 --> 00:15:21.659
I really need to take him home.

381
00:15:21.833 --> 00:15:23.705
-Oh. sure.
-Let's go. sweetheart.

382
00:15:23.835 --> 00:15:25.533
Oh. and also...

383
00:15:25.663 --> 00:15:27.448
...these googly
eyes sure are fun.

384
00:15:28.492 --> 00:15:29.885
What's that about?

385
00:15:30.016 --> 00:15:31.582
I couldn't tell you. Good night.

386
00:15:31.713 --> 00:15:33.933
Night. Let's go.

387
00:15:36.065 --> 00:15:37.719
It's true. No prints anywhere.

388
00:15:37.849 --> 00:15:39.634
Somebody may have
wiped them down.

389
00:15:39.721 --> 00:15:42.071
So this wasn't an unfortunate
necktie shredding accident?

390
00:15:42.202 --> 00:15:45.161
I'll admit. Ms. Tascioni
makes some good points.

391
00:15:45.335 --> 00:15:48.425
Well. that'll save time.
Elsbeth. what's your theory?

392
00:15:54.649 --> 00:15:56.390
And that's for you.

393
00:15:59.784 --> 00:16:01.612
I have gifts!

394
00:16:01.743 --> 00:16:04.441
Okay.

395
00:16:04.572 --> 00:16:06.095
This is for you.

396
00:16:06.182 --> 00:16:08.489
-You didn't have to do that.
-Oh. I wouldn't dream

397
00:16:08.619 --> 00:16:10.795
of coming back from
overseas empty-handed.

398
00:16:10.882 --> 00:16:12.623
Okay. Lt. Connor.

399
00:16:12.754 --> 00:16:14.886
this had your name on it.

400
00:16:17.193 --> 00:16:19.108
Just right. Thank you. Elsbeth.

401
00:16:19.239 --> 00:16:20.936
You are so welcome.

402
00:16:21.067 --> 00:16:22.851
Oh. Captain Wagner.

403
00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:24.853
I know how much you
love your whiskey.

404
00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:27.856
Duty free. which I thought
was ironic for you.

405
00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:29.945
Bannerdale 18. Very nice.

406
00:16:30.076 --> 00:16:31.472
-Thank you. Elsbeth.
-You're welcome.

407
00:16:31.555 --> 00:16:35.255
And Bobby... shortbread.

408
00:16:35.342 --> 00:16:36.343
Oh.

409
00:16:36.473 --> 00:16:38.171
Oh. Officer Hackett. obviously.

410
00:16:38.301 --> 00:16:40.216
I didn't know you yet. but

411
00:16:40.347 --> 00:16:43.524
I got a bunch of
these adorable erasers

412
00:16:43.654 --> 00:16:46.135
that look like
hairy Highland coos.

413
00:16:46.309 --> 00:16:48.181
That better be a kind of cow.

414
00:16:48.311 --> 00:16:50.792
-There you go! There's one for you.
-Whoa!

415
00:16:50.966 --> 00:16:52.663
-Ooh!
-Whoa. So. how's the jet lag?

416
00:16:52.794 --> 00:16:53.925
You okay to work?

417
00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:55.536
Oh. yes. yes. I just need

418
00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.060
my first big cup of coffee.

419
00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.411
Hey. we pay for coffee now?

420
00:17:01.542 --> 00:17:02.978
We have continued
to look at ways

421
00:17:03.109 --> 00:17:04.066
to follow new budget guidelines.

422
00:17:04.153 --> 00:17:06.721
Which is his oh-so-polite
way of saying.

423
00:17:06.808 --> 00:17:09.115
"We've got nothing for you
anymore. deal with it."

424
00:17:09.289 --> 00:17:11.682
Well. I'm sure it's
not Lt. Connor's fault.

425
00:17:11.769 --> 00:17:13.728
Huh. Yeah. Well...

426
00:17:13.858 --> 00:17:15.904
he's the numbers guy.

427
00:17:16.035 --> 00:17:19.299
It's true. I am.

428
00:17:21.518 --> 00:17:23.128
Does anyone have a dollar?

429
00:17:23.303 --> 00:17:26.306
Okay. I would put my
thoughts down on cards.

430
00:17:26.435 --> 00:17:28.438
but. um...

431
00:17:28.612 --> 00:17:31.224
there seem to be no more
cards in the supply closet.

432
00:17:31.354 --> 00:17:32.881
which is fine because
I'm on the wait list

433
00:17:32.964 --> 00:17:34.183
-for a Sharpie.
-How are those

434
00:17:34.357 --> 00:17:35.706
numbers working out?

435
00:17:35.837 --> 00:17:39.623
Clearly. this was
not an accident.

436
00:17:39.754 --> 00:17:42.670
We agree. So. who
had it in for him?

437
00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:44.585
Well. maybe Mickey didn't
just find the body.

438
00:17:44.759 --> 00:17:46.543
I mean. the guy was
humiliated by Bristol

439
00:17:46.717 --> 00:17:47.979
every night for years.

440
00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:49.242
Wasn't that the bit?

441
00:17:49.372 --> 00:17:51.113
The experience can
still feel real.

442
00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.419
I don't know.

443
00:17:52.549 --> 00:17:53.598
Mickey seemed pretty broken up

444
00:17:53.681 --> 00:17:55.074
over Scotty's death.

445
00:17:55.204 --> 00:17:56.296
Finished
putting all the papers

446
00:17:56.379 --> 00:17:57.946
in the shredder back together.

447
00:17:58.033 --> 00:17:59.774
It was like that
scene from Argo.

448
00:17:59.861 --> 00:18:03.560
Mm. Yeah. that is the one thing
I remember from that movie.

449
00:18:03.691 --> 00:18:04.866
And it won Best Picture.

450
00:18:04.996 --> 00:18:06.346
Uh. what did you find?

451
00:18:06.476 --> 00:18:07.782
Uh. it was a packet...

452
00:18:07.869 --> 00:18:10.219
jokes submitted by
an aspiring writer

453
00:18:10.393 --> 00:18:11.873
looking for a job on the show.

454
00:18:12.003 --> 00:18:15.311
I actually submitted
a few myself.

455
00:18:15.442 --> 00:18:17.317
You know. I swear they
used a joke of mine once.

456
00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.750
they just changed
Pelosi to Beyoncé.

457
00:18:19.837 --> 00:18:22.318
And they didn't give you
any money? Or credit?

458
00:18:22.492 --> 00:18:24.842
Well. I believe the
contractual term is "bupkis."

459
00:18:24.973 --> 00:18:27.062
Well. sounds like Scotty
Bristol must have pissed off

460
00:18:27.236 --> 00:18:29.760
a lot of writers. Maybe
one of them wanted revenge.

461
00:18:29.847 --> 00:18:31.414
Mm. not likely.

462
00:18:31.545 --> 00:18:32.633
And why not?

463
00:18:32.807 --> 00:18:34.635
Well. I mean. most
comedy writers

464
00:18:34.809 --> 00:18:37.377
would take Scotty Bristol
stealing one of their jokes

465
00:18:37.507 --> 00:18:40.249
as encouragement to keep going.

466
00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:41.468
We're a sad bunch.

467
00:18:41.642 --> 00:18:43.252
Well. what about the
writers on the show?

468
00:18:43.383 --> 00:18:45.211
How do they feel about
Scotty stealing jokes

469
00:18:45.341 --> 00:18:46.995
and feeding theirs
to a giant shredder?

470
00:18:47.169 --> 00:18:48.344
Exactly.

471
00:18:48.475 --> 00:18:50.129
We need to talk to them.

472
00:18:51.913 --> 00:18:53.440
And if you look to your
right. you'll see the office

473
00:18:53.523 --> 00:18:57.223
where our host. Scotty
Bristol. was found dead.

474
00:18:57.353 --> 00:18:59.573
That must have
been hard for you.

475
00:18:59.703 --> 00:19:01.444
You know. it was.

476
00:19:01.575 --> 00:19:03.925
I know he had a
mixed reputation.

477
00:19:04.099 --> 00:19:05.709
but Scotty was
always so nice to me.

478
00:19:05.883 --> 00:19:09.104
He told me all about his
early days doing improv.

479
00:19:09.235 --> 00:19:11.106
It's amazing what
people will tell a page.

480
00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:13.413
He'd reminisce whenever I
went in to empty Mickey Two.

481
00:19:13.543 --> 00:19:14.543
Mickey Two?

482
00:19:14.631 --> 00:19:15.763
Oh. that's everybody's

483
00:19:15.893 --> 00:19:16.590
nickname for the shredder.

484
00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.374
It's kinda mean.

485
00:19:18.461 --> 00:19:20.246
Did you always empty Mickey Two?

486
00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:21.595
That's what Scotty wanted.

487
00:19:21.725 --> 00:19:23.249
I'm the only
non-janitor with a key

488
00:19:23.379 --> 00:19:25.294
to Scotty's and
Laurel's offices.

489
00:19:25.381 --> 00:19:28.079
The two of them were touchy
about their shredders.

490
00:19:28.167 --> 00:19:31.344
Maybe because Scotty
liked to steal material.

491
00:19:32.693 --> 00:19:34.869
-This business.
-Well. what can you

492
00:19:34.999 --> 00:19:36.871
tell us about Scotty
and the shredder?

493
00:19:36.958 --> 00:19:40.527
Oh. Mickey Two? He liked to fire
it up to remind us who's boss.

494
00:19:40.614 --> 00:19:43.269
That's a funny nickname
for a shredder. though.

495
00:19:43.399 --> 00:19:46.228
Well. we named it Mickey Two.
like Audrey Two in Little Shop.

496
00:19:46.315 --> 00:19:47.625
because just like
the real Mickey.

497
00:19:47.708 --> 00:19:48.988
Scotty made it eat crap all day.

498
00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:52.191
Did Laurel know the nickname?

499
00:19:52.365 --> 00:19:55.585
Oh. yes. but she would never
laugh. because she's management.

500
00:19:55.716 --> 00:19:58.980
Or maybe because you were all
making fun of her husband.

501
00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:00.550
Well. that's the
sentimental version.

502
00:20:00.721 --> 00:20:02.853
We found a writer's packet
in Scotty's shredder.

503
00:20:02.984 --> 00:20:04.420
Duh. Of course you did.

504
00:20:04.507 --> 00:20:05.987
Well. him
using that stuff

505
00:20:06.117 --> 00:20:07.902
must have really burned
you guys up. huh?

506
00:20:07.989 --> 00:20:09.168
He should have trusted
the professionals.

507
00:20:09.251 --> 00:20:10.383
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

508
00:20:10.513 --> 00:20:11.906
Did it make you
want to get even?

509
00:20:13.516 --> 00:20:15.039
Wait.

510
00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:16.867
We thought this was an accident.

511
00:20:16.998 --> 00:20:18.238
Is this a murder investigation?

512
00:20:18.347 --> 00:20:21.481
It had to be Ronan.
It's so obvious.

513
00:20:21.568 --> 00:20:23.439
He wanted Scotty's job.

514
00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.706
-Come on. he's the guy.
-Steph! Steph slept with Scotty

515
00:20:25.789 --> 00:20:27.795
at the last season wrap party and
ever since then -JIM: Oh. that's true.

516
00:20:27.878 --> 00:20:29.402
She became totally obsess...

517
00:20:29.532 --> 00:20:31.172
-obsessive.
-Shut up. That is just stupid.

518
00:20:31.273 --> 00:20:32.974
-Suspect.
-But I actually bet it was you that killed him.

519
00:20:33.057 --> 00:20:34.672
-Wouldn't sleep with you. and I mostly...
-You guys...

520
00:20:34.755 --> 00:20:36.191
Guys. stop!

521
00:20:36.322 --> 00:20:37.322
This is not a bit.

522
00:20:38.541 --> 00:20:41.501
You mind telling us where
you were last night?

523
00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:44.678
Yes. I did two sets

524
00:20:44.765 --> 00:20:46.205
at Mr. Titters...
club in the Village.

525
00:20:46.288 --> 00:20:48.464
Oh. right. yes.
we were all there.

526
00:20:48.551 --> 00:20:49.900
Both sets. cheering him on.

527
00:20:50.031 --> 00:20:51.554
Really? All of you?

528
00:20:51.685 --> 00:20:53.208
Both sets? Why?

529
00:20:53.339 --> 00:20:55.776
Well. we were sucking
up to Ronan in case

530
00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:58.257
he gets Scotty's
job. Which. now.

531
00:20:58.387 --> 00:21:00.824
he will. because I
missed my moment.

532
00:21:00.911 --> 00:21:02.826
So. congratulations.

533
00:21:02.957 --> 00:21:04.567
-Very happy for you.
-Yeah.

534
00:21:04.698 --> 00:21:07.135
They have video
cameras at Mr. Titters.

535
00:21:07.309 --> 00:21:09.050
You can see the audience.

536
00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:11.099
I'm sure we got filmed during
our good-natured heckling.

537
00:21:11.182 --> 00:21:12.532
Well. we'll double-check.

538
00:21:12.662 --> 00:21:14.403
'cause it does seem
awfully convenient.

539
00:21:14.577 --> 00:21:16.579
I mean. you guys all
clearly had a problem

540
00:21:16.753 --> 00:21:17.928
working for Scotty Bristol.

541
00:21:18.059 --> 00:21:19.408
so maybe you all

542
00:21:19.539 --> 00:21:22.019
worked together to murder
him and cover it up.

543
00:21:22.193 --> 00:21:24.152
Detective. you
got to understand.

544
00:21:24.326 --> 00:21:25.588
We're writers.

545
00:21:25.762 --> 00:21:27.547
We would never do
anything to rock the boat.

546
00:21:27.677 --> 00:21:29.466
It's true. This is a
hostile work environment.

547
00:21:29.549 --> 00:21:32.378
but we are all so
grateful to have a job.

548
00:21:32.508 --> 00:21:34.205
This business.

549
00:21:38.079 --> 00:21:39.950
Which one is that?

550
00:21:40.081 --> 00:21:41.822
Uh. benazepril.

551
00:21:41.952 --> 00:21:44.085
Uh. it's the. uh. ACE inhibitor.

552
00:21:44.215 --> 00:21:46.174
They don't work if you
forget to take them.

553
00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:48.219
Well. that's what
I've got you for.

554
00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:50.831
Mickey...

555
00:21:50.961 --> 00:21:52.963
why did you go back to
Scotty's office last night?

556
00:21:53.094 --> 00:21:55.139
I told you to go home.

557
00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:57.751
I was gonna give
him an ultimatum.

558
00:21:57.881 --> 00:22:00.580
Either I get the time off
so I can take care of myself

559
00:22:00.754 --> 00:22:02.321
or I quit.

560
00:22:02.408 --> 00:22:04.105
I mean. it wasn't fair to me

561
00:22:04.192 --> 00:22:06.760
or to you anymore.

562
00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:08.370
I'd had it.

563
00:22:09.415 --> 00:22:11.765
Then I never got the chance.

564
00:22:13.723 --> 00:22:16.117
Oh.

565
00:22:16.247 --> 00:22:17.988
Oh. Mickey.

566
00:22:18.162 --> 00:22:20.295
Oh. I wish I'd known that.

567
00:22:23.429 --> 00:22:25.126
What is he doing?

568
00:22:25.256 --> 00:22:28.216
Looks like he's psyching
himself up for something.

569
00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:29.739
Yeah.

570
00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:31.350
To murder someone.

571
00:22:38.357 --> 00:22:40.228
I almost
quit all the time.

572
00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:41.795
I just never went
through with it.

573
00:22:41.882 --> 00:22:43.322
Yeah. but this time
you didn't just quit.

574
00:22:43.405 --> 00:22:44.928
You murdered Scotty
for making you

575
00:22:45.102 --> 00:22:46.713
a laughingstock in
front of millions.

576
00:22:46.843 --> 00:22:49.542
You
know nothing about comedy.

577
00:22:49.672 --> 00:22:51.282
Geez. I get no respect.

578
00:22:51.457 --> 00:22:53.459
Um. what about you?

579
00:22:53.589 --> 00:22:55.243
Did you want Mickey to quit?

580
00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:58.115
I wanted what was best
for Mickey. That's all.

581
00:22:58.289 --> 00:22:59.726
This interview is over.

582
00:22:59.856 --> 00:23:02.337
Mickey. go home and call
Edward. That's our lawyer.

583
00:23:02.468 --> 00:23:04.905
Clearly. the police want to
waste their time focusing on

584
00:23:05.079 --> 00:23:07.081
Scotty's best
friend in the world.

585
00:23:07.211 --> 00:23:09.083
This is unbelievable.

586
00:23:09.213 --> 00:23:10.824
We'll be in touch.

587
00:23:10.954 --> 00:23:12.220
In the meantime. we'll
have another chat

588
00:23:12.303 --> 00:23:14.349
with building security.

589
00:23:14.480 --> 00:23:15.829
I'll catch up with you later.

590
00:23:18.701 --> 00:23:20.834
Hey. Laurel. Laurel.

591
00:23:20.964 --> 00:23:22.401
Um. I just want you to know

592
00:23:22.531 --> 00:23:24.185
I think the police
have this wrong.

593
00:23:24.359 --> 00:23:25.843
I don't think Mickey
could have done this.

594
00:23:25.926 --> 00:23:28.494
-You're smart.
-The thing is. I would love it

595
00:23:28.624 --> 00:23:31.235
if you would help
me figure this out

596
00:23:31.322 --> 00:23:33.324
to clear your husband's name.

597
00:23:33.412 --> 00:23:35.414
Would you be willing to do that?

598
00:23:35.544 --> 00:23:37.372
How can I say no?

599
00:23:37.546 --> 00:23:39.069
Oh. Great.

600
00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:40.248
'Scuse me. Laurel.

601
00:23:40.331 --> 00:23:42.943
Wow. boy.

602
00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:45.989
-You have a tough job.
-How do you mean?

603
00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:48.339
Well. the writers think
of you as management.

604
00:23:48.470 --> 00:23:49.819
Well. they blame
everything on me.

605
00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:51.560
That's how Scotty liked it.

606
00:23:51.647 --> 00:23:54.824
Oh. and Scotty... doesn't
sound like he was an easy boss.

607
00:23:54.955 --> 00:23:57.305
And then to watch what the
show was doing to your husband

608
00:23:57.436 --> 00:24:00.221
every night? Laurel.
you juggle a lot.

609
00:24:00.351 --> 00:24:03.833
Well. you juggle a lot. too. or
you wouldn't carry so many bags.

610
00:24:04.007 --> 00:24:05.792
True.

611
00:24:05.922 --> 00:24:08.969
Although I don't have to
think about my husband. Ex.

612
00:24:09.099 --> 00:24:12.842
Although he did just
narrowly escape disbarment.

613
00:24:13.016 --> 00:24:14.453
Not sure how I feel about that.

614
00:24:14.583 --> 00:24:16.672
I'm sorry. but I have
an awful lot to do.

615
00:24:16.846 --> 00:24:19.109
Oh. of course. Um. what
are you working on?

616
00:24:19.240 --> 00:24:21.242
We're preparing a
tribute show for Scotty.

617
00:24:21.372 --> 00:24:23.897
Oh. And who knew him
better than you did?

618
00:24:24.027 --> 00:24:25.681
Uh. by the way.

619
00:24:25.812 --> 00:24:29.076
did Scotty also call
the shredder Mickey Two

620
00:24:29.250 --> 00:24:31.644
or was that just the writers?

621
00:24:33.384 --> 00:24:35.299
You knew all about that.

622
00:24:35.386 --> 00:24:37.345
Right?

623
00:24:37.476 --> 00:24:38.655
And yet you acted
like you didn't

624
00:24:38.738 --> 00:24:41.088
when I asked you
about the... grr!

625
00:24:41.262 --> 00:24:43.220
Googly eyes at the crime scene.

626
00:24:43.307 --> 00:24:45.745
You taking about the
night of the accident?

627
00:24:45.832 --> 00:24:48.269
You asked me and I said.
"I couldn't tell you."

628
00:24:48.399 --> 00:24:50.445
I couldn't tell you because
Mickey was right there

629
00:24:50.619 --> 00:24:52.273
and I didn't want
to hurt his feelings

630
00:24:52.403 --> 00:24:54.275
or make him look
guilty. God forbid.

631
00:24:54.405 --> 00:24:55.668
So. I couldn't tell you.

632
00:24:56.756 --> 00:24:58.453
Wow. you're awfully
quick on your feet.

633
00:24:58.584 --> 00:25:00.020
Must be my improv training.

634
00:25:00.150 --> 00:25:01.587
Oh. right.

635
00:25:02.675 --> 00:25:04.372
Carl. cue it up
to the beginning.

636
00:25:04.503 --> 00:25:06.156
You got it.

637
00:25:06.287 --> 00:25:07.553
So cool.

638
00:25:07.636 --> 00:25:09.203
Wow.

639
00:25:09.333 --> 00:25:10.813
Oh. hey.

640
00:25:10.987 --> 00:25:12.423
Is that you?

641
00:25:12.554 --> 00:25:14.295
That's. uh. that's

642
00:25:14.425 --> 00:25:16.732
Scotty and Mickey
and you. isn't it?

643
00:25:16.863 --> 00:25:19.300
Yeah. we were in a group
called The Overalls.

644
00:25:19.430 --> 00:25:22.564
Oh. that explains the outfits.

645
00:25:22.695 --> 00:25:25.785
That is so fun.

646
00:25:25.872 --> 00:25:27.787
You guys were a big
hit. weren't you?

647
00:25:33.662 --> 00:25:34.881
We didn't know what we were.

648
00:25:35.011 --> 00:25:37.231
We were just having fun

649
00:25:37.318 --> 00:25:39.015
and making each other laugh.

650
00:25:39.146 --> 00:25:40.582
Three kids in Seattle

651
00:25:40.756 --> 00:25:44.020
just loving each other
and what we were doing.

652
00:25:44.151 --> 00:25:46.370
That. of course. was
before the jealousy

653
00:25:46.457 --> 00:25:48.590
and the deals and show business.

654
00:25:48.721 --> 00:25:51.245
Mm. Before you knew that. uh.

655
00:25:51.419 --> 00:25:53.813
Scotty would be the star?

656
00:25:53.943 --> 00:25:56.903
Oh. we always knew that.

657
00:25:57.033 --> 00:25:59.035
Boy.

658
00:25:59.122 --> 00:26:01.211
I would love to
learn how to do that.

659
00:26:01.298 --> 00:26:03.257
What. improv?

660
00:26:03.344 --> 00:26:05.476
No. it's not much
of a thing anymore.

661
00:26:05.651 --> 00:26:07.740
But it's such an
important skill.

662
00:26:07.914 --> 00:26:10.046
And it would be so
useful in my work.

663
00:26:10.133 --> 00:26:13.920
I could probably use it to
find Scotty's real killer.

664
00:26:14.094 --> 00:26:15.617
T.

665
00:26:15.704 --> 00:26:17.053
U.

666
00:26:17.184 --> 00:26:18.359
V.

667
00:26:18.533 --> 00:26:19.534
W!

668
00:26:19.665 --> 00:26:20.665
X.

669
00:26:20.753 --> 00:26:21.971
Y?!

670
00:26:22.102 --> 00:26:23.494
Z.

671
00:26:23.582 --> 00:26:24.974
Okay. All ri...

672
00:26:25.148 --> 00:26:26.759
You see how we're
more connected now?

673
00:26:26.889 --> 00:26:28.195
Yes. I do.

674
00:26:28.369 --> 00:26:30.197
I feel like I can
almost read your mind.

675
00:26:30.371 --> 00:26:32.286
Okay. let's try a
more advanced game.

676
00:26:32.416 --> 00:26:33.679
All right. let's do

677
00:26:33.766 --> 00:26:35.550
-Questions Only.
-Okay.

678
00:26:35.637 --> 00:26:38.118
Now. everything you say must
be in the form of a question.

679
00:26:38.248 --> 00:26:40.076
Mm-hmm. Ooh! Like Jeopardy!

680
00:26:40.207 --> 00:26:42.513
Uh. yeah. Yeah. like Jeopardy!

681
00:26:42.601 --> 00:26:45.560
Okay. and remember the first
rule of improv: "Yes. and."

682
00:26:45.647 --> 00:26:47.431
You never deny what
the other person says

683
00:26:47.562 --> 00:26:48.781
because it kills the scene.

684
00:26:48.955 --> 00:26:51.087
You go along with it and
you add new information

685
00:26:51.174 --> 00:26:52.567
so the scene builds.

686
00:26:52.698 --> 00:26:54.003
-Oh. All right.
-Okay. yeah.

687
00:26:54.177 --> 00:26:57.137
So. uh. let's start with
a place for the scene.

688
00:26:57.267 --> 00:26:58.225
Uh... Ooh!

689
00:26:58.312 --> 00:26:59.748
A Renaissance fair.

690
00:26:59.879 --> 00:27:01.620
Hm. Well. what made
you come up with that?

691
00:27:01.794 --> 00:27:03.796
Did you know that was a
bit we did in The Overalls?

692
00:27:03.970 --> 00:27:05.754
Yes. and...

693
00:27:05.885 --> 00:27:08.583
I've done a
bunch of research on you.

694
00:27:08.757 --> 00:27:10.193
Was that good?

695
00:27:10.324 --> 00:27:11.978
Yeah. well. we haven't
really started yet.

696
00:27:12.108 --> 00:27:13.893
-Oh.
-Okay? So let's start now.

697
00:27:14.023 --> 00:27:15.986
-Okay. Okay. Sorry. sorry.
-All right.

698
00:27:16.069 --> 00:27:17.461
So. here we go. Um...

699
00:27:17.636 --> 00:27:19.899
Is this your first time
at the Renaissance fair?

700
00:27:20.029 --> 00:27:21.029
Uh...

701
00:27:21.161 --> 00:27:22.031
Does it look like

702
00:27:22.205 --> 00:27:24.338
my first time. lassie?

703
00:27:24.425 --> 00:27:27.428
Lassie? Okay. well. yes.
that was a question.

704
00:27:27.602 --> 00:27:29.038
but it didn't add
new information.

705
00:27:29.212 --> 00:27:30.696
So. what it did was
it threw the question

706
00:27:30.779 --> 00:27:32.955
back on me. so now I'm
doing all the work.

707
00:27:33.042 --> 00:27:34.478
-Oh.
-Yeah.

708
00:27:34.609 --> 00:27:37.394
Oh. I see. Gosh. yeah. I...

709
00:27:37.568 --> 00:27:40.571
I tend to do that with people.

710
00:27:40.659 --> 00:27:43.792
Okay. oh... L-Let... let
me try-let me try it again.

711
00:27:43.966 --> 00:27:44.967
Okay.

712
00:27:45.141 --> 00:27:46.490
Yes.

713
00:27:46.665 --> 00:27:48.797
Do
you like my breeches?

714
00:27:48.928 --> 00:27:50.190
Uh. okay. good.

715
00:27:50.364 --> 00:27:51.844
Um. yes. I love them.

716
00:27:52.018 --> 00:27:53.846
-and would you like to dance?
-Ooh!

717
00:27:53.976 --> 00:27:56.196
Absolutely. I wouldst.

718
00:27:56.283 --> 00:27:57.980
-Oh. we're dancing.
-And...

719
00:27:58.154 --> 00:28:00.330
uh. but. um...

720
00:28:00.461 --> 00:28:03.029
will your husband mind?

721
00:28:03.159 --> 00:28:04.683
Mm. Okay.

722
00:28:04.857 --> 00:28:07.686
"But" is okay if it
keeps adding information.

723
00:28:07.816 --> 00:28:10.558
which you did. And yes. he will.

724
00:28:10.689 --> 00:28:12.821
-Will you tell him?
-Yes.

725
00:28:12.952 --> 00:28:16.477
but wouldst thou
secretly murder me first?

726
00:28:19.436 --> 00:28:20.790
Did I do it wrong?

727
00:28:20.873 --> 00:28:22.396
No. it's just a
little confusing.

728
00:28:22.526 --> 00:28:24.224
with all the "wouldst's."

729
00:28:26.052 --> 00:28:27.706
I really have to get
back to the edit.

730
00:28:27.836 --> 00:28:30.056
-Oh. shoot. Are you sure?
-Yes.

731
00:28:30.186 --> 00:28:32.754
And?

732
00:28:32.885 --> 00:28:35.409
Yes. and that was
a very good start.

733
00:28:35.496 --> 00:28:38.151
You're very quick
on your feet. too.

734
00:28:38.281 --> 00:28:39.979
But you need more practice.

735
00:28:43.417 --> 00:28:44.853
Didn't we
already see this?

736
00:28:44.940 --> 00:28:46.424
Oh. he's wearing
different clothes.

737
00:28:46.507 --> 00:28:49.728
I wanted to test Mickey's
story. so I did some research.

738
00:28:49.858 --> 00:28:51.251
There's a fan online
who's compiled

739
00:28:51.381 --> 00:28:52.643
all the most humiliating

740
00:28:52.774 --> 00:28:54.558
Mickey Muntz
moments on the show.

741
00:28:54.689 --> 00:28:57.823
Oh. there were so many. The
lint suit. the snake tank.

742
00:28:57.953 --> 00:28:59.132
And then I got the
security footage

743
00:28:59.215 --> 00:29:00.564
from after those tapings.

744
00:29:00.695 --> 00:29:02.653
Sure enough. half the time.

745
00:29:02.741 --> 00:29:05.178
Mickey was in the elevator.
working himself up

746
00:29:05.308 --> 00:29:08.572
to almost quit.
just like he said.

747
00:29:08.703 --> 00:29:09.878
Which shows...

748
00:29:10.009 --> 00:29:11.057
-He did it!
-He didn't do it.

749
00:29:11.140 --> 00:29:13.142
Oh. come on. He did it!

750
00:29:13.316 --> 00:29:15.231
-He didn't do it.
-He absolutely did it.

751
00:29:15.362 --> 00:29:17.020
-He di-he didn't do it.
-Come on. come on. Elsbeth.

752
00:29:17.103 --> 00:29:18.586
-gimme a break.
-Ah. ah. ah. ah. ah. ah. ah!

753
00:29:18.669 --> 00:29:19.932
-One at a time.
-Okay. Captain.

754
00:29:20.062 --> 00:29:21.934
the security footage
clearly shows

755
00:29:22.108 --> 00:29:24.110
a years-long process of Mickey

756
00:29:24.240 --> 00:29:26.242
building up the courage
to murder Scotty.

757
00:29:26.373 --> 00:29:27.461
Yes. and...

758
00:29:27.548 --> 00:29:29.028
it shows a weak man

759
00:29:29.158 --> 00:29:30.642
who would never hurt
the boss he worshipped.

760
00:29:30.725 --> 00:29:32.814
-Why "yes. and"?
-What?

761
00:29:32.945 --> 00:29:33.993
You just completely
contradicted me

762
00:29:34.076 --> 00:29:35.730
but you started with "Yes. and."

763
00:29:35.861 --> 00:29:37.061
Oh. it's better for the scene.

764
00:29:37.166 --> 00:29:38.341
We're in a scene?

765
00:29:38.472 --> 00:29:40.082
Seeing Mickey go
through all that

766
00:29:40.213 --> 00:29:41.997
was painful to watch.

767
00:29:42.128 --> 00:29:44.695
but it must have been even more
painful for his wife. Laurel.

768
00:29:44.826 --> 00:29:46.610
especially given
Mickey's bad heart.

769
00:29:46.741 --> 00:29:48.177
But everything you say

770
00:29:48.308 --> 00:29:50.919
also points to Mickey.
and he found the body.

771
00:29:51.006 --> 00:29:54.009
Yes. and it points
just as much to Laurel.

772
00:29:54.140 --> 00:29:55.968
And why are you
carrying a waste basket?

773
00:29:56.098 --> 00:29:58.144
To make a point. Hey! Connor.

774
00:29:59.275 --> 00:30:01.103
-You see this?
-Garbage?

775
00:30:01.234 --> 00:30:03.410
Yeah. the same garbage that's
been here for three days.

776
00:30:03.540 --> 00:30:06.282
Yes. it has been necessary to
scale back trash collection.

777
00:30:06.456 --> 00:30:08.636
Oh. no. no. do-don... don't
hide behind the passive voice.

778
00:30:08.719 --> 00:30:11.070
I should be able to eat a
banana and not worry about

779
00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:14.116
the peel sticking around
long enough to grow fuzz.

780
00:30:15.770 --> 00:30:18.207
Are you gonna do
something about this?

781
00:30:18.381 --> 00:30:20.862
Nope. Mmm.

782
00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:25.824
What did Edward have to say?

783
00:30:25.954 --> 00:30:28.870
Uh. he told me he's gonna
put me in touch with a lawyer

784
00:30:29.044 --> 00:30:30.872
-who handles this sort of thing.
-When?

785
00:30:31.003 --> 00:30:32.961
I-I don't know. Tomorrow. maybe.

786
00:30:33.092 --> 00:30:34.692
Maybe? The police are
not fooling around.

787
00:30:34.789 --> 00:30:37.444
Why didn't you tell them
that you wanted me to quit?

788
00:30:40.969 --> 00:30:42.105
What... what-what
are you saying?

789
00:30:42.188 --> 00:30:43.363
The police asked you

790
00:30:43.537 --> 00:30:45.191
and you lied.

791
00:30:45.321 --> 00:30:46.975
I didn't lie.

792
00:30:47.106 --> 00:30:48.977
I told them I wanted
what was best for you.

793
00:30:49.064 --> 00:30:50.892
and that's true. that's
always been true.

794
00:30:52.894 --> 00:30:56.245
Laurel. were you in the
edit that whole time?

795
00:30:56.376 --> 00:30:59.031
Don't do this. Mickey.

796
00:30:59.161 --> 00:31:00.815
-You're just torturing
yourself -Oh...

797
00:31:00.946 --> 00:31:02.469
and me.

798
00:31:02.643 --> 00:31:06.125
You lied. You did
want me to quit.

799
00:31:06.212 --> 00:31:08.910
I wanted you to get time off.

800
00:31:09.084 --> 00:31:10.694
And now you have it.
And you can use it

801
00:31:10.869 --> 00:31:12.522
to get better and
to do great things.

802
00:31:12.653 --> 00:31:14.481
But without Scotty?

803
00:31:14.611 --> 00:31:16.396
I...

804
00:31:16.526 --> 00:31:18.267
Laurel. I...

805
00:31:18.398 --> 00:31:20.139
Mi-Mickey? Mickey!

806
00:31:21.618 --> 00:31:25.144
So. he couldn't bear the guilt
of killing Scotty Bristol

807
00:31:25.231 --> 00:31:28.495
and his heart gave out.
huh? Is that about it?

808
00:31:28.625 --> 00:31:30.584
Yes. and...

809
00:31:30.671 --> 00:31:32.629
that's exactly what he told me

810
00:31:32.760 --> 00:31:35.023
just before he died.

811
00:31:40.681 --> 00:31:41.987
Think before you write.

812
00:31:42.117 --> 00:31:44.859
Crossing something
out is a waste of ink.

813
00:31:50.821 --> 00:31:52.649
-Captain Wagner.
-Mm?

814
00:31:52.780 --> 00:31:55.696
Are you fully aware of
what's going on out there?

815
00:31:55.826 --> 00:31:57.654
To what are you referring?

816
00:31:57.741 --> 00:32:01.136
These budget cuts... they're
so arbitrary and absurd.

817
00:32:01.267 --> 00:32:03.182
and everyone's taking
it out on Lt. Connor.

818
00:32:03.312 --> 00:32:05.619
Yes. And?

819
00:32:05.706 --> 00:32:08.796
Well. I have seen. recently.

820
00:32:08.927 --> 00:32:10.972
what can happen when a person's

821
00:32:11.103 --> 00:32:13.061
put in that position.

822
00:32:13.192 --> 00:32:16.325
It's not fair and it
leads to bad things.

823
00:32:16.499 --> 00:32:18.066
Part of being a good boss

824
00:32:18.197 --> 00:32:20.677
is effectively delegating
responsibility.

825
00:32:20.851 --> 00:32:22.244
Connor can handle it.

826
00:32:22.375 --> 00:32:23.898
What about his feelings?

827
00:32:24.029 --> 00:32:26.205
-Connor has feelings?
-Captain.

828
00:32:26.379 --> 00:32:28.337
You know what else is
part of being a good boss?

829
00:32:28.511 --> 00:32:30.774
Taking the blame when necessary.

830
00:32:30.905 --> 00:32:32.428
You... Come.

831
00:32:32.559 --> 00:32:34.213
The report's in.
Uh. Mickey Muntz

832
00:32:34.343 --> 00:32:36.432
died of a catastrophic coronary.

833
00:32:36.563 --> 00:32:37.912
No sign of foul play.

834
00:32:38.086 --> 00:32:41.263
Okay. Case closed.

835
00:32:41.394 --> 00:32:43.226
We have some of his
personal effects to return

836
00:32:43.309 --> 00:32:46.094
to the widow. His
watch. uh. wedding ring.

837
00:32:46.225 --> 00:32:48.488
Oh. I can take them
to her. If that helps.

838
00:32:48.662 --> 00:32:51.230
Yeah. Thank you.

839
00:32:52.709 --> 00:32:56.539
You aren't done. are you?

840
00:32:58.411 --> 00:33:01.066
Cameron.

841
00:33:01.196 --> 00:33:03.285
Have you heard anything
from our friend?

842
00:33:03.416 --> 00:33:06.158
I'm not supposed to
say anything. Uh. d...

843
00:33:06.288 --> 00:33:07.946
I can't believe that Kaya
wouldn't want me to know

844
00:33:08.029 --> 00:33:10.162
she's okay. Oh!
I said her name.

845
00:33:10.336 --> 00:33:12.136
Are-are we not supposed
to be saying her name?

846
00:33:12.251 --> 00:33:13.992
Uh. we both know her name.

847
00:33:14.122 --> 00:33:15.515
-So. when...
-No. I. um...

848
00:33:15.689 --> 00:33:18.561
So. I have spoken to her.

849
00:33:18.735 --> 00:33:21.173
and she completed
training and has begun

850
00:33:21.347 --> 00:33:23.218
her first undercover assignment.

851
00:33:23.349 --> 00:33:26.569
And she sounds pretty
damn happy about it.

852
00:33:26.700 --> 00:33:28.876
Oh. That's good.

853
00:33:28.963 --> 00:33:29.877
Yes.

854
00:33:30.008 --> 00:33:32.053
Tell her that there's a plushie

855
00:33:32.227 --> 00:33:34.273
Loch Ness Monster
with her name on it.

856
00:33:34.403 --> 00:33:36.101
-Okay. I'll let her know.
-Okay.

857
00:33:36.231 --> 00:33:37.711
And that concludes

858
00:33:37.841 --> 00:33:39.582
our tribute to the
great Scotty Bristol.

859
00:33:39.713 --> 00:33:41.062
In the meantime...

860
00:33:41.193 --> 00:33:43.064
I just don't think I
should do the tie bit.

861
00:33:43.238 --> 00:33:44.330
It was Scotty's thing.

862
00:33:44.413 --> 00:33:45.936
Are you gonna fight
me on everything?

863
00:33:46.067 --> 00:33:47.329
Hi. Laurel.

864
00:33:48.722 --> 00:33:50.419
Take a break. We'll
argue about this later.

865
00:33:50.550 --> 00:33:51.855
Looking forward.

866
00:33:51.986 --> 00:33:54.902
Your deal hasn't closed yet.

867
00:33:55.033 --> 00:33:56.382
Surprised to see you here.

868
00:33:56.556 --> 00:33:58.514
We're reworking
the tribute show.

869
00:33:58.601 --> 00:33:59.994
cutting out any trace of Mickey.

870
00:34:00.125 --> 00:34:02.170
Oh. right. because
Mickey killed him.

871
00:34:02.344 --> 00:34:04.912
You know you didn't
have to tell the police

872
00:34:05.043 --> 00:34:08.045
that Mickey confessed. There's
still spousal privilege.

873
00:34:08.176 --> 00:34:09.525
You could have kept his secret.

874
00:34:09.656 --> 00:34:12.050
I know. But I couldn't
bear to see someone else

875
00:34:12.179 --> 00:34:13.790
take the blame for
Scotty's murder.

876
00:34:13.964 --> 00:34:16.184
Of course.

877
00:34:16.315 --> 00:34:17.925
That makes total sense.

878
00:34:18.056 --> 00:34:19.753
Thanks for bringing these.

879
00:34:23.190 --> 00:34:25.193
You know. there's something else

880
00:34:25.324 --> 00:34:26.889
I was wondering about.

881
00:34:27.065 --> 00:34:30.197
-What's that?
-Well. Detective Smullen

882
00:34:30.329 --> 00:34:32.547
thinks Mickey's heart gave out

883
00:34:32.679 --> 00:34:35.551
because he couldn't bear
the secret guilt anymore.

884
00:34:35.638 --> 00:34:37.335
But if he confessed to you.

885
00:34:37.422 --> 00:34:39.077
then that burden was removed.

886
00:34:39.206 --> 00:34:41.208
so why did he have
a heart attack?

887
00:34:41.340 --> 00:34:43.864
I mean. exactly when
did Mickey confess...

888
00:34:43.994 --> 00:34:45.474
was it before the
attack or during?

889
00:34:45.605 --> 00:34:47.607
Because it certainly
couldn't have been after.

890
00:34:47.694 --> 00:34:49.870
Mickey knew Scotty
was in love with me.

891
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:51.614
He thought we were having
an affair and I couldn't

892
00:34:51.697 --> 00:34:54.004
convince him that we
weren't. That's why.

893
00:34:54.135 --> 00:34:56.355
I see.

894
00:34:56.485 --> 00:34:57.965
Wow.

895
00:34:58.096 --> 00:35:00.576
You just added new information
in just the right spot.

896
00:35:00.750 --> 00:35:03.840
So. um...

897
00:35:03.971 --> 00:35:05.886
did anything ever happen

898
00:35:06.016 --> 00:35:08.454
between you and Scotty. say.

899
00:35:08.628 --> 00:35:09.542
in his office?

900
00:35:09.629 --> 00:35:11.370
No.

901
00:35:11.500 --> 00:35:13.241
No?

902
00:35:13.415 --> 00:35:15.591
Not "Yes. and"?

903
00:35:17.158 --> 00:35:18.638
No.

904
00:35:38.223 --> 00:35:40.094
Can I have your
attention. please?

905
00:35:42.488 --> 00:35:44.577
I know things are tough.

906
00:35:44.707 --> 00:35:46.622
And we've had to make some

907
00:35:46.709 --> 00:35:48.537
painful adjustments.

908
00:35:48.668 --> 00:35:52.280
But in case you haven't noticed.
that is happening all over.

909
00:35:52.411 --> 00:35:54.674
And the work that we do

910
00:35:54.804 --> 00:35:56.676
is too important

911
00:35:56.806 --> 00:35:58.895
to focus on

912
00:35:59.026 --> 00:36:01.594
petty inconveniences.

913
00:36:02.638 --> 00:36:05.250
We will get through this
difficult time together.

914
00:36:05.380 --> 00:36:06.947
But in the meantime.

915
00:36:07.077 --> 00:36:08.731
if you have a complaint...

916
00:36:12.213 --> 00:36:14.563
...you come to me.

917
00:36:33.974 --> 00:36:37.412
Hey. this isn't my trash.

918
00:36:41.199 --> 00:36:43.940
Very funny. Detective Smullen.

919
00:36:49.990 --> 00:36:52.297
That's it.

920
00:37:12.099 --> 00:37:14.406
I know you did it for him.

921
00:37:14.536 --> 00:37:15.842
I'm sorry?

922
00:37:15.972 --> 00:37:17.713
I'm sure you are.

923
00:37:17.844 --> 00:37:19.802
About part of it.
anyway. I mean.

924
00:37:19.976 --> 00:37:23.110
you didn't know that things
would turn out this way.

925
00:37:23.241 --> 00:37:25.982
You and Mickey and Scotty...

926
00:37:26.069 --> 00:37:28.333
you had a special bond.

927
00:37:28.463 --> 00:37:31.292
just like the characters
in Merrily We Roll Along.

928
00:37:31.379 --> 00:37:33.207
Scotty's favorite musical.

929
00:37:33.338 --> 00:37:36.471
under appreciated until
the recent revival.

930
00:37:37.211 --> 00:37:38.517
Is there a point to this?

931
00:37:38.647 --> 00:37:40.301
Yes.

932
00:37:40.432 --> 00:37:42.651
Because that bond

933
00:37:42.782 --> 00:37:46.046
also gave you power
over each other.

934
00:37:46.176 --> 00:37:48.570
And Scotty used that power

935
00:37:48.701 --> 00:37:50.093
to control your lives.

936
00:37:50.268 --> 00:37:52.792
like when he told
you not to have kids.

937
00:37:52.879 --> 00:37:55.098
or when he wouldn't give Mickey

938
00:37:55.273 --> 00:37:57.405
the break his doctors ordered.

939
00:37:57.492 --> 00:38:00.190
Well... How do
you know all that?

940
00:38:00.321 --> 00:38:02.323
It's amazing what
people will tell a page.

941
00:38:02.454 --> 00:38:04.499
And Scotty told me a lot.

942
00:38:04.673 --> 00:38:06.458
Your plan was
to make it look like

943
00:38:06.588 --> 00:38:09.461
an unfortunate
shredding accident.

944
00:38:09.591 --> 00:38:11.027
I mean. after all.

945
00:38:11.158 --> 00:38:13.900
Scotty loved to torture
the writers with the...

946
00:38:14.030 --> 00:38:15.597
...noise.

947
00:38:15.728 --> 00:38:17.991
But there was no one
there to hear it.

948
00:38:18.165 --> 00:38:19.427
And...

949
00:38:19.558 --> 00:38:22.038
we pieced the shredded
pages back together.

950
00:38:22.169 --> 00:38:23.910
It was a packet that had

951
00:38:24.040 --> 00:38:26.521
no jokes used on
the show that night.

952
00:38:26.652 --> 00:38:29.350
So why was Scotty shredding?

953
00:38:29.524 --> 00:38:31.352
Well. I don't know.
I wasn't there.

954
00:38:31.483 --> 00:38:33.963
Oh. see. now. that's
not good improv.

955
00:38:34.050 --> 00:38:35.487
A better move

956
00:38:35.661 --> 00:38:38.577
was when you tried to
pin the murder on Mickey

957
00:38:38.707 --> 00:38:41.580
after he died. Except the killer

958
00:38:41.710 --> 00:38:43.059
had to...

959
00:38:43.233 --> 00:38:46.149
tighten Scotty's tie

960
00:38:46.324 --> 00:38:49.283
and then lure him
over to the shredder

961
00:38:49.457 --> 00:38:51.154
without any sign of a struggle.

962
00:38:51.285 --> 00:38:54.288
Mickey couldn't have
done that. But you could.

963
00:38:54.419 --> 00:38:57.639
using your 30 years of history

964
00:38:57.726 --> 00:39:00.642
and a little alcohol...

965
00:39:00.729 --> 00:39:04.690
...to manipulate
Scotty into position.

966
00:39:06.082 --> 00:39:07.693
Oh. this is ludicrous.

967
00:39:07.823 --> 00:39:11.044
Yeah. maybe. But
it was a pretty good plan.

968
00:39:11.131 --> 00:39:13.481
Until after the
murder. when you saw

969
00:39:13.612 --> 00:39:16.919
that the shredder bin was empty.
thanks to Matthew the page.

970
00:39:17.050 --> 00:39:18.965
I never forgot to
empty Mickey Two.

971
00:39:19.095 --> 00:39:21.276
It couldn't look like
an accident if there wasn't

972
00:39:21.359 --> 00:39:22.838
shredded paper in the bin.

973
00:39:22.925 --> 00:39:26.059
And you couldn't use Mickey
Two 'cause Scotty's body...

974
00:39:26.146 --> 00:39:27.626
...was in the way.

975
00:39:27.756 --> 00:39:31.151
So you ran back to your office.

976
00:39:31.281 --> 00:39:32.979
you shredded the
latest packet...

977
00:39:34.502 --> 00:39:37.026
...and you brought that

978
00:39:37.157 --> 00:39:39.768
and put it in Scotty's bin.

979
00:39:39.899 --> 00:39:43.206
Detective Smullen tried
a similar trick on me.

980
00:39:43.337 --> 00:39:44.599
which made me think of it.

981
00:39:44.730 --> 00:39:46.340
For which I have apologized.

982
00:39:46.427 --> 00:39:48.864
Well. you
can't prove any of this.

983
00:39:48.995 --> 00:39:51.301
Oh. actually. we can.

984
00:39:51.389 --> 00:39:53.826
Because it turns out. uh...

985
00:39:53.956 --> 00:39:56.611
No
two shredders are the same.

986
00:39:56.742 --> 00:39:59.005
The width between the
blades on Mickey Two

987
00:39:59.179 --> 00:40:01.703
was a quarter of an
inch further apart

988
00:40:01.790 --> 00:40:05.403
than the blades on the
shredder in your office.

989
00:40:05.533 --> 00:40:07.666
And only you and
Matthew the page

990
00:40:07.753 --> 00:40:11.409
had keys to have access
both of the shredders.

991
00:40:11.583 --> 00:40:12.975
But Matthew was
with the writers.

992
00:40:13.106 --> 00:40:15.891
watching Ronan Gaines doing
standup at Mr. Titters.

993
00:40:16.022 --> 00:40:17.327
I was sucking up.

994
00:40:17.458 --> 00:40:19.678
It had
to be you. Laurel.

995
00:40:21.941 --> 00:40:24.465
You and Mickey and Scotty...

996
00:40:24.596 --> 00:40:27.163
you were old friends.

997
00:40:27.294 --> 00:40:29.470
Now two of you are dead.

998
00:40:31.037 --> 00:40:32.125
I didn't kill Mickey.

999
00:40:32.299 --> 00:40:34.562
Not directly. no.

1000
00:40:35.737 --> 00:40:37.130
Uh...

1001
00:40:37.304 --> 00:40:39.088
We had a good thing going.

1002
00:40:39.219 --> 00:40:40.742
Mm.

1003
00:40:42.701 --> 00:40:44.616
Ma'am. This way. please.

1004
00:40:51.318 --> 00:40:53.363
You really do know everything

1005
00:40:53.494 --> 00:40:55.409
that goes on around
here. don't you?

1006
00:40:55.540 --> 00:40:58.717
You could say that
and be correct.

1007
00:41:00.022 --> 00:41:01.502
Could you do me a favor?

1008
00:41:02.677 --> 00:41:05.550
Get your Way Late with Scotty
Bristol office supplies.

1009
00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:07.856
They don't want 'em anymore.
Too depressing.

1010
00:41:09.771 --> 00:41:11.686
-Thank you. Elsbeth.
-Mm.

1011
00:41:13.645 --> 00:41:16.735
But I'm still gonna
use my bagpipe stapler.

1012
00:41:23.350 --> 00:41:24.873
Thank you for bringing all that.

1013
00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:26.879
It should help calm things
down here for a while.

1014
00:41:26.962 --> 00:41:28.529
Of course.

1015
00:41:28.660 --> 00:41:31.967
But. uh. you know. the
box wasn't that big.

1016
00:41:32.054 --> 00:41:33.926
The trouble isn't just over.

1017
00:41:34.056 --> 00:41:35.231
I know.

1018
00:41:35.362 --> 00:41:36.672
Well. maybe you
should rethink things.

1019
00:41:36.755 --> 00:41:37.973
No.

1020
00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:39.540
That's not possible.

1021
00:41:39.671 --> 00:41:41.586
-Uh. but. I...
-Elsbeth.

1022
00:41:41.716 --> 00:41:44.066
it was either those cuts

1023
00:41:44.197 --> 00:41:46.068
or get rid of you.

1024
00:41:46.199 --> 00:41:48.288
And that is not

1025
00:41:48.418 --> 00:41:50.420
something I would entertain.

1026
00:41:57.079 --> 00:41:58.603
-Hey.
-Oh. hey.

1027
00:41:58.733 --> 00:42:00.082
Thanks for a fun time.

1028
00:42:00.213 --> 00:42:01.693
You actually inspired me.

1029
00:42:01.823 --> 00:42:03.651
-Really?
-In fact.

1030
00:42:03.782 --> 00:42:05.740
I submitted another
packet to Way Late

1031
00:42:05.871 --> 00:42:09.396
and Ronan Gaines bought
one of my jokes for $200.

1032
00:42:09.527 --> 00:42:10.919
Oh! He did?

1033
00:42:11.050 --> 00:42:14.096
-Yeah.
-That's so good. Oh. wow.

1034
00:42:14.227 --> 00:42:16.142
See? The top job

1035
00:42:16.272 --> 00:42:19.493
doesn't automatically
make someone a monster.

1036
00:42:21.669 --> 00:42:24.237
Oh. this business.

1037
00:42:26.587 --> 00:42:28.284
Okay. So. now

1038
00:42:28.415 --> 00:42:30.939
let's introduce
my new sidekick...

1039
00:42:31.070 --> 00:42:34.116
the only idiot willing to
take this humiliating job...

1040
00:42:34.247 --> 00:42:36.167
Matthew the Way Late Page!

1041
00:42:36.292 --> 00:42:39.078
Thank you. sir. So
glad to be here. Ronan.

1042
00:42:39.208 --> 00:42:41.519
We like to promote from
within. We don't like to pay you more.

1043
00:42:41.602 --> 00:42:43.517
and we haven't. but
glad you're aboard.

1044
00:42:43.604 --> 00:42:45.644
Can I get you anything?

